From: Johannes Meyer zum Alten Borgloh <code@jzab.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:43:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] (hybris) Camera: expose physical cameras of logical
 multi-cameras to API1

droidmedia, and with it gst-droid and the Sailfish camera app, only uses
camera API1. filterLogicalCameraIdsLocked keeps one API1 ID per facing out
of each logical camera and its physical cameras, so on pdx246 (logical
cameras 3 and 4 over the main camera 0 and the ultra-wide 2) API1 saw only
cameras 0 and 1 and the ultra-wide was unreachable.

Under persist.camera.api1.expose_physical (default true), keep the
physical cameras and drop a logical camera whose physical cameras are all
listed; pdx246 then exposes 0, 1 and 2. The idea comes from sharks-dev's
"Fix camera1 API" gist (Mister_Magister) for the Xperia 10 IV/10 V ports,
which skips this filter entirely under the same property; here the
logical cameras are dropped as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I24c911c34a4453638f6e64eda2a577d6327a6109
---
 .../common/CameraProviderManager.cpp          | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/camera/libcameraservice/common/CameraProviderManager.cpp b/services/camera/libcameraservice/common/CameraProviderManager.cpp
index 7032db04aa..fd2b359f38 100644
--- a/services/camera/libcameraservice/common/CameraProviderManager.cpp
+++ b/services/camera/libcameraservice/common/CameraProviderManager.cpp
@@ -3580,6 +3580,27 @@ status_t CameraProviderManager::getCameraCharacteristicsLocked(const std::string
 void CameraProviderManager::filterLogicalCameraIdsLocked(
         std::vector<std::string>& deviceIds) const
 {
+    // (hybris) droidmedia only speaks camera API1. Expose the physical cameras
+    // of a logical multi-camera (pdx246: the ultra-wide, camera 2, behind the
+    // logical cameras 3 and 4) and drop a logical camera whose physical cameras
+    // are all listed. Idea from sharks-dev's "Fix camera1 API" gist
+    // (Mister_Magister) for the Xperia 10 IV/10 V ports, which skips this filter
+    // entirely under the same property.
+    if (property_get_bool("persist.camera.api1.expose_physical", true)) {
+        const std::unordered_set<std::string> listed(deviceIds.begin(), deviceIds.end());
+        deviceIds.erase(std::remove_if(deviceIds.begin(), deviceIds.end(),
+                [this, &listed](const std::string& id) {
+                    auto info = findDeviceInfoLocked(id);
+                    if (info == nullptr || !info->mIsLogicalCamera) return false;
+                    return std::all_of(info->mPhysicalIds.begin(), info->mPhysicalIds.end(),
+                            [&listed](const std::string& p) { return listed.count(p) > 0; });
+                }), deviceIds.end());
+        std::string s;
+        for (auto& id : deviceIds) s += " " + id;
+        ALOGI("%s: API1 camera ids:%s", __FUNCTION__, s.c_str());
+        return;
+    }
+
     // Map between camera facing and camera IDs related to logical camera.
     std::map<int, std::unordered_set<std::string>> idCombos;
 
